" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">programming languages<\/a>, making it efficient and beginner-friendly.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Features &amp; Uses:<\/strong><\/h4>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Rich Libraries:<\/strong> Python offers powerful libraries like Pandas, NumPy, Matplotlib, and Scikit-learn for data manipulation, visualization, and machine learning.<br><\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>AI &amp; ML Applications<\/strong>: It has become one of the leading\u2002languages for <a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/what-is-artificial-intelligence\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">artificial intelligence (AI)<\/a> and machine learning (ML).<br><\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Database &amp; Cloud Integration<\/strong>: Python seamlessly connects with databases and cloud services, making it ideal for big data processing.<br><\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>High Scalability<\/strong>: Suitable for handling large datasets and complex computations.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Drawbacks:<\/strong><\/h4>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Execution Speed: <\/strong>Python is an interpreted language and is slower than compiled\u2002languages like <a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/resources\/cpp\/what-is-cpp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">C++<\/a>.<br><\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Data Visualization Limitations<\/strong>: While Python has visualization tools, it often requires additional libraries and setup.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Best For:<\/strong><\/h4>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Data\u2002Analysts &amp; ML Engineers: <\/strong>Best for structured and unstructured data.<br><\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Routine tasks automated data analysis:<\/strong> In web scraping, data\u2002cleaning, data mining, and automation.<br><\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Beginners<\/strong>: Its readable syntax makes it an excellent choice for learning programming and data science.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>8. SAS<\/strong><\/h3>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-full is-resized\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"512\" height=\"210\" src=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/03\/sas.webp\" alt=\"SAS\" class=\"wp-image-13355\" style=\"width:232px;height:auto\" srcset=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/03\/sas.webp 512w, https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/03\/sas-300x123.webp 300w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 512px) 100vw, 512px\" \/><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<p>SAS (Statistical Analysis System) is a data analytics software suite for data management, statistical analysis, predictive analytics, and business intelligence. It is used in industries that demand advanced data modelling, particularly in finance, healthcare, and governance.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Features &amp; Uses:<\/strong><\/h4>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>AI-Powered Analytics:<\/strong> Provides support for ML, AI and deep\u2002Learning models.<br><\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Industry-Specific Implementations:<\/strong> Widely\u2002utilized in sectors such as healthcare, finance, marketing, and risk management for making data-driven decisions.<br><\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Robust Data Security &amp; Compliance:<\/strong> Meets industry regulations, making it ideal for handling sensitive data.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Drawbacks:<\/strong><\/h4>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>High Licensing Costs:<\/strong> Expensive for small businesses and individuals, making it more suitable for large enterprises.<br><\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Limited Open-Source Support:<\/strong> SAS has a much smaller developer community and fewer free learning resources than open-source tools\u2002like R or Python.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Best For:<\/strong><\/h4>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Enterprises with Structured Data Needs:<\/strong> Ideal for organizations handling large and complex structured datasets.<br><\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Financial Services and Healthcare: <\/strong>Commonly used\u2002for regulatory compliance, fraud detection, and risk assessment.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Businesses Requiring High Security in Analytics:<\/strong> Suitable for companies that need strong data governance and protection.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>9. Qlik Sense<\/strong><\/h3>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-full is-resized\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"389\" height=\"129\" src=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/03\/qlik-sense.webp\" alt=\"Qlik Sense\" class=\"wp-image-13380\" style=\"width:259px;height:auto\" srcset=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/03\/qlik-sense.webp 389w, https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/03\/qlik-sense-300x99.webp 300w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 389px) 100vw, 389px\" \/><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<p>Qlik Sense is a self-service data visualization and business intelligence tool that allows organizations to get AI-powered insights for better decision-making. It\u2002provides strong data analysis capabilities and interactive dashboards, which makes it a popular choice among business analysts.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Features &amp; Uses:<\/strong><\/h4>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Dynamic Data Exploration:<\/strong>\u2002Enables users to navigate data dynamically without prior queries.<br><\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Interactive Dashboards and Reports: <\/strong>You can dive deep into data and visualize business trends in detail.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Drawbacks:<\/strong><\/h4>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>High Enterprise Costs:<\/strong> The pricing can be high, which might make it less affordable for small businesses.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Requires Advanced Knowledge for Complex Queries:<\/strong> While data pooling is easy, in-depth analytics require expertise.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Best For:<\/strong><\/h4>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Enterprises Seeking AI-Powered Business Intelligence:<\/strong> Ideal for organizations needing data-driven decision-making.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Business Analysts:<\/strong> This is a good solution for professionals who\u2002require interactive and self-service analytics.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Also read:<\/strong> <a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/data-analytics-books\/\">10 Best Data Analytics Books You Should Read<\/a><\/p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>10. KNIME<\/strong><\/h3>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-full\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"311\" height=\"162\" src=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/03\/knime.webp\" alt=\"knime\" class=\"wp-image-13381\" srcset=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/03\/knime.webp 311w, https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/03\/knime-300x156.webp 300w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 311px) 100vw, 311px\" \/><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<p>KNIME stands\u2002for Konstanz Information Miner and is an open-source data analytics, machine learning and workflow automation platform. It offers an intuitive drag-and-drop interface for users to create elaborate data pipelines\u2002without requiring much coding experience. KNIME is popular across\u2002industries for data preprocessing, predictive modeling, and training machine learning models.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Features &amp; Uses:<\/strong><\/h4>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Visual\u2002Workflow Builder: <\/strong>Build and manage data workflows using a no-code interface.<br><\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Seamless integration: \u2002<\/strong>compatible with Python, R, SQL, Hadoop, Spark and other big data tools.<br><\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Data mining is very powerful: <\/strong>Utilized\u2002in predictive analysis, clustering, classification and anomaly detection.<br><\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Automation &amp; Scalability: <\/strong>Automates repetitive data processes and runs smoothly with larger data sets\u2002via extensions.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Drawbacks:<\/strong><\/h4>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>It is slow when processing large datasets<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Requires plugins for additional functionality<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Best For:<\/strong><\/h4>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Data scientists and machine learning engineers<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Organizations requiring workflow automation<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Predictive modeling with open-source flexibility<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"has-white-color has-vivid-cyan-blue-background-color has-text-color has-background has-link-color wp-elements-ccc32798605aa1e3b4a19d0b260b90ec\"><strong>Explore Our Data Related Courses<\/strong><\/p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table\"><table class=\"has-fixed-layout\"><tbody><tr><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\"><a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/data-analytics-course?utm_source=WsBlog&amp;utm_medium=BlogInterlink&amp;utm_campaign=seo\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Data Analytics Course<\/a><\/td><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\">Live Internship + 100% Job Support<\/td><\/tr><tr><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\"><a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/business-analytics-course?utm_source=WsBlog&amp;utm_medium=BlogInterlink&amp;utm_campaign=seo\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Business Analytics Course<\/a><\/td><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\">Live Internship + 100% Job Support<\/td><\/tr><tr><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\"><a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/data-science-course?utm_source=WsBlog&amp;utm_medium=BlogInterlink&amp;utm_campaign=seo\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Data Science Course<\/a><\/td><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\">Live Internship + 100% Job Support<\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>How do you choose the <\/strong><strong>best tool for data analytics<\/strong><strong>?<\/strong><\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p>Choosing the best data analytics tool depends on your needs and expertise:<\/p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Business Intelligence &amp; Reporting<\/strong>: If you need interactive dashboards and reports, go for Power BI or Tableau (great for visualizing data).<br><\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Big Data Processing<\/strong>: If you\u2019re dealing with massive datasets, Hadoop and Apache Spark are the best choices for distributed computing.<br><\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>AI &amp; Machine Learning<\/strong>: If your focus is predictive modeling, automation, or deep learning, choose TensorFlow, Python, or KNIME.<br><\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Ease of Use<\/strong>: If you prefer a no-code or low-code tool, Power BI, Tableau, and KNIME are user-friendly.<br><\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>For Developers &amp; Data Scientists<\/strong>: If you have coding skills, Python, R, or Spark offer flexibility and customization.<br><\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Budget Considerations<\/strong>: Python, KNIME, and Hadoop are free, while Power BI and Tableau have paid plans with advanced features.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>FAQs About Data Analytics Tools<\/strong><\/h2>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"schema-faq wp-block-yoast-faq-block\"><div class=\"schema-faq-section\" id=\"faq-question-1742312555357\"><strong class=\"schema-faq-question\"><strong>What are data analytics tools\u2002used for?<\/strong><\/strong> <p class=\"schema-faq-answer\"><strong>Data analytics tools <\/strong>analyze, visualize, and process large volumes of data to extract insights, make\u2002data-driven decisions, and\/or optimize business performance.<\/p> <\/div> <div class=\"schema-faq-section\" id=\"faq-question-1742312566255\"><strong class=\"schema-faq-question\"><strong>Which is the best\u2002tool for big data analytics?<\/strong><\/strong> <p class=\"schema-faq-answer\">Apache\u2002Spark and Hadoop are the best options for processing large data sets efficiently.<\/p> <\/div> <div class=\"schema-faq-section\" id=\"faq-question-1742312578262\"><strong class=\"schema-faq-question\"><strong>Is Python\u2002suitable for data analysis?<\/strong><\/strong> <p class=\"schema-faq-answer\">Yes, Python can be useful for data analytics. Its libraries, such as Pandas,\u2002Numpy, and Matplotlib, allow for the manipulation and visualization of data.<\/p> <\/div> <div class=\"schema-faq-section\" id=\"faq-question-1742312590519\"><strong class=\"schema-faq-question\"><strong>Which Data Analytics Tool\u2002Should I Choose?<\/strong><\/strong> <p class=\"schema-faq-answer\">Evaluate aspects like the complexity of your data, usability, its capability to integrate with other platforms, pricing, and what your analytics require,\u2002among others.<\/p> <\/div> <div class=\"schema-faq-section\" id=\"faq-question-1742312602536\"><strong class=\"schema-faq-question\"><strong>What are the disadvantages of\u2002data analytics tools?<\/strong><\/strong> <p class=\"schema-faq-answer\">Disadvantages\u2002include expensive prices, a highly complex learning curve, low performance, and the requirement for technical knowledge.<\/p> <\/div> <div class=\"schema-faq-section\" id=\"faq-question-1742312614276\"><strong class=\"schema-faq-question\"><strong>What analytics\u2002tools do you have for free?<\/strong><\/strong> <p class=\"schema-faq-answer\">Of\u2002course, there are free versions of analytics tools such as KNIME, Google Data Studio, R, and Python.<\/p> <\/div> <\/div>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-full\"><a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/data-analytics-course?utm_source=WsBlog&amp;utm_medium=BlogBanner&amp;utm_campaign=seo&amp;utm_page=\/data-analytics-tools\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1546\" height=\"381\" src=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/09\/da-course-3.webp\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-12832\" srcset=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/09\/da-course-3.webp 1546w, https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/09\/da-course-3-300x74.webp 300w, https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/09\/da-course-3-1024x252.webp 1024w, https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/09\/da-course-3-768x189.webp 768w, https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/09\/da-course-3-1536x379.webp 1536w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1546px) 100vw, 1546px\" \/><\/a><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Conclusion<\/strong><\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>Data analytics tools help you turn raw data into useful insights. Whether you need simple charts or advanced machine learning, there\u2019s a tool for every task. If you\u2019re a beginner, start with easy tools like Python or Power BI. For big data, try Apache Spark or Hadoop. If you\u2019re working on AI or machine learning, TensorFlow and Python are great choices. The best tool depends on your goals, the size of your data, and your skills. By picking the right tool, you can make smarter decisions and grow your business.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"has-white-color has-vivid-cy